# Code owners for ValoReview.
#
# One line, and deliberately so: this repository has a single contributor, so
# per-directory rules would name the same person ten times and drift the first
# time a path moved. Split this up when there is a second owner to name.
#
# What this file buys today is automatic review requests on every pull request
# into a protected branch, which is a reminder rather than a gate.
#
# It is NOT safe to pair with "Require review from Code Owners" in branch
# protection while the owner is one person: GitHub does not let you approve
# your own pull request, so requiring an owner's review on a solo repository
# leaves no path to merge. Turn that setting on when a second owner exists.

